f AAIH-Mn and AAIH-Co, and add it into 3 mL of water-saturated n-octanol solution or 3 mL of n-octanol-saturated aqueous solution, respectively. Subsequently, the resulting mixture was placed on a stirrer at r.t. for 5–7 h. After the complex was completely dissolved in the mixture solution (with no solid precipitate observed), it was allowed to stand for layer separation. Pipetted 50 μL from both the n-octanol layer and the aqueous layer respectively, and then add 950 μL of nitric acid to fully digest the samples. Then further pipetted 50 μL of the digested sample and add 950 μL of redistilled water to afford a diluted sample solution, which was submitted for the determination of the metal ion content using ICP–MS."}],"ccdc":["ABOCEE"]}